{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.LeviFormDefect","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.LeviFormDefect","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Set.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.matterLocus_proper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.matterLocus_proper","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L149-L160","doc":"**The matter locus is a proper, non-empty subset.**\n\nThis is the first statement in the file that no field contains: `nondeg`\nsupplies the left half, and bilinearity — which nothing assumes about the\nlocus — supplies the right. A defect *locus* that were empty or that were\nthe whole space would not be a locus, and neither is excluded by the\nstructure's fields alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.matterLocus_ne_univ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.matterLocus_ne_univ","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L141-L147","doc":"The matter locus is not everything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.zero_right_notMem_matterLocus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.zero_right_notMem_matterLocus","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L136-L139","doc":"The matter locus misses the zero section in the second argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.zero_left_notMem_matterLocus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.zero_left_notMem_matterLocus","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L130-L134","doc":"The matter locus misses the zero section in the first argument: bilinearity\nforces `ℒ(0, y) = 0`. Derived, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.matter_locus_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.matter_locus_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L122-L128","doc":"The matter locus is non-empty — one step from `nondeg`, but about the\ndefined set rather than a restatement of the field's type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.matterLocus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.matterLocus","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L109-L120","doc":"**The matter locus** `Sing(λ)`: the pairs at which the Levi form fails to\nvanish.\n\nThe `.md` defines matter as this set — *\"the set of such points forms the\nmatter locus `Sing(λ) ⊂ Spec(A)`\"* — and until 2026-09-03 it had no\ncounterpart in the Lean, so a theorem could name it without any object to\nbe about. It lives in `carrier × carrier` rather than in a spectrum; see\nthe module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.nondeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.nondeg","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L105-L105","doc":"Non-degeneracy: there exists a point where the Levi form is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.leviForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.leviForm","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The Levi form as a bilinear map (abstracting T^{1,0} × T^{0,1} → k). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.modulInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.modulInst","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L100-L100","doc":"Module structure on the carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.addCommInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.addCommInst","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Additive structure on the carrier (presupposed by the module structure). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.carrier","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The ambient algebra (spectral fiber).  Pinned to `Type v` per §7d U2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect.mk","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LeviFormDefect","kind":"structure","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.lean#L88-L105","doc":"The Levi form defect structure: captures the failure of the\nFrobenius form at a point in the spectral fiber.\n\nAt a point p, the Levi form ℒ_p measures non-degeneracy of the\ncontact structure. The matter locus is the set of points where\nℒ_p ≠ 0. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:levi-form-defect","label":"def:levi-form-defect","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/levi-form-defect.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}